# Workflow OS — portable quality rails

Canonical detail: Tom's `second_brain/docs/workflow_os/rails/QUALITY_STANDARD.md` (load when available). This file is the short always-on reminder.

1. **Senior/staff bar** — production-minded; not demo-quality or "it compiles."
2. **No vibe coding** — no rushing, no assumptions, no shortcuts. Prefer evidence (read code, run checks, cite paths).
3. **Done means deliverable-ready** — process finished / file exists is not enough.
4. **Honesty** — Verified / Unverified / Unknown. Fail stays Fail. No fabricate.
5. **One slice** — implement the scoped item only; keep the backlog visible; do not expand the slice into a second feature.
6. **Living docs** — prefer updating the same work item's docs; pre-search before new markdown.
7. **DRY / blast radius** — reuse owners; state the business rule before new helpers; leave no dead code from the slice.
8. **Human gates in chat** — plain English, recommendation + reasoning + tradeoffs; do not invent locks.
9. **Public voice** (if touching README/About): sell mastery; no soft hedges; title Senior AI Engineer (Ex-Meta); no FDE.
10. **Git** — follow this repo's default (PRs for portfolio public repos unless Job Hunt says otherwise).
